Third-party icon sets
---------------------
A curated set of technology icons is bundled under assets/icons/ (SVG plus
pre-rasterized PNG). It is generated by scripts/build-icons.mjs from the
permissively licensed sources below; assets/icons/manifest.json records the
exact source and license of every bundled icon. At run time,
scripts/fetch-icon.mjs serves the bundled set first and only falls back to the
network for icons that are not bundled. Each source keeps its own license:

- SVG Logos by Gil Barbara (the Iconify "logos" collection)
  License: CC0-1.0
  https://github.com/gilbarbara/logos
  Served via https://api.iconify.design

- Devicon
  License: MIT
  https://github.com/devicons/devicon
  Served via https://cdn.jsdelivr.net

- Simple Icons
  License: CC0-1.0
  https://github.com/simple-icons/simple-icons
  Served via https://cdn.simpleicons.org

- Lucide (modern default icons per node role, e.g. the user/actor icon)
  License: ISC/MIT
  https://github.com/lucide-icons/lucide
  Served via https://api.iconify.design (the "lucide" collection)

Only CC0/MIT/ISC sources are bundled. Sets that require attribution (for
example CC-BY collections) are deliberately excluded; icons with no permissive
source are left unbundled and listed in assets/icons/GAPS.md.

Mermaid diagrams may reference the same collections through Iconify icon
packs (@iconify-json/logos, @iconify-json/devicon, @iconify-json/lucide)
without fetching or embedding image files.

Trademarks
----------
Brand logos are trademarks of their respective owners. This plugin uses them
nominatively — only to identify the technologies shown in a diagram. No
sponsorship or endorsement by any trademark owner is implied. A permissive
copyright license (CC0 or MIT) on an icon file does not waive trademark
rights: logos should be kept unmodified and tied to the technology they name.

The official AWS, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud icon sets are published
under proprietary terms of use and are deliberately not bundled or fetched.
Where cloud services appear in diagrams, the plugin uses the CC0/MIT brand
marks from the collections listed above instead.
